From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 02:02:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] feat(suzanne1): the 40x40 ASCII arena joins the machinery
 run
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The machinery course revived the Suzanne1.*.x study; this composes the OTHER
Suzanne record — the authored 40x40 Suzanne1.ASCII arena (in-repo bytes,
64ec6746…) whose NOT_REVIVED verdict asked for exactly 'a composed v2 scene
where the chains and pistons can exist'. The ledger's claim that Suzanne 1
'plays its exact 40x40 arena' becomes true with this commit.

archive-suzanne1-scene.ts builds it from the decoded record — every position
the archive's own number under one declared mapping ((p - 20) x 2.4): 208 wall
cubes DYNAMIC as archived (a pushable maze is the arena's signature) in their
recorded per-symbol textures (objet39 / Podium / grass), the three archived
pistons as kinematic movers between the archived ±0.5 limits along the archived
orientations (constant-speed drive disclosed adapted — the original used
asymmetric slider-joint forces), 45 chain assemblies as static stands (same
joint-vocabulary disclosure), 15 ZRing pickups at the archived 0.1°/ms spin,
LINE gates spanning the archived post pairs (the halfway line runs its full
recorded diagonal), laps: 3, and the recovered two-body ball the record itself
binds (internalTexture: FireArrow800.jpg). Absent and recorded: CubX anchors,
the unconverted XML airplane, the unrecoverable random humans.

The texture registry gains the recovered Suzanne1 set (objet39, podium,
grass-sample, z-ring) and concrete (the source2017 floor binding). Games shelf
entry beside the machinery run; __GRAPHYSX_ARCHIVE__.composeSuzanne1 for agents.

Verified: new smoke-suzanne1 in the gate — census exact (208/208 dynamic walls,
135 chain bodies, 15 rings, 3 kinematic plates, 2 gates, 4 posts), a piston
plate proven to move along its archived axis under deterministic stepping with
zero cross-axis drift, ball rests, all rings collect, the run completes over
3 laps, and the document round-trips. Screenshot: suzanne1-arena.png.

